WEBVTT

01:19.300 --> 01:21.260
KATSUTA SAUCE

01:41.400 --> 01:43.160
Half a cabbage,

01:43.400 --> 01:46.120
potatoes, onions,

01:47.660 --> 01:48.640
and carrots.

01:50.580 --> 01:52.020
Miss Maid.

01:52.220 --> 01:53.520
Are you making curry today?

01:53.520 --> 01:54.260
Ah.

01:54.260 --> 01:55.640
It seems so.

01:55.640 --> 01:56.920
It's nice.

01:56.920 --> 01:58.820
Get you some more vegetables.

01:59.880 --> 02:00.960
Well,

02:04.300 --> 02:05.360
well…

02:06.120 --> 02:08.840
Is there something you need from me?

02:08.840 --> 02:09.620
WelI…

02:09.620 --> 02:11.940
I've always been paying attention to you.

02:12.280 --> 02:14.460
I think you are really beautiful.

02:14.940 --> 02:17.160
I want to be like you.

02:17.600 --> 02:18.900
It's my honor.

02:18.900 --> 02:20.160
So, I want to ask

02:20.540 --> 02:23.860
where you bought this outfit.

02:24.040 --> 02:25.520
My outfit?

02:25.520 --> 02:26.900
Mm.

02:27.160 --> 02:29.940
I've been thinking I'd ask you
if I got the chance.

02:29.940 --> 02:32.120
Because this outfit

02:32.120 --> 02:34.000
is not something
ordinary people would wear.

02:35.120 --> 02:38.599
So, I wonder if I could be
as beautiful as you wearing it.

02:43.940 --> 02:45.500
Miss Yuki.

02:46.240 --> 02:47.840
Master Hitoyoshi.

02:48.720 --> 02:49.880
What a coincidence.

02:50.260 --> 02:51.620
I am going to the bookstore.

02:53.260 --> 02:56.380
Isn't a maid's outfit an ordinary outfit?

03:00.910 --> 03:07.290
(You Are Ms. Servant.)

04:29.500 --> 04:31.950
(Episode 7: You've Finally Noticed it.)
So, we decided to go shopping on Sunday

04:32.080 --> 04:34.820
to buy casual clothes for Miss Yuki.

04:34.820 --> 04:36.040
OGISO STATION

04:37.300 --> 04:39.300
Hello.

04:39.300 --> 04:40.240
Hmm?

04:40.240 --> 04:41.960
Over here.

04:41.960 --> 04:43.480
She is…

04:45.820 --> 04:48.890
Because you sent me a message,
so I came here.

04:48.890 --> 04:52.350
Do you know what clothes would suit Miss Yuki?
We are going to buy clothes.

04:52.680 --> 04:56.040
I am available on Sunday.

04:56.540 --> 04:58.700
Wait, I know why you came.

04:58.980 --> 05:00.300
But why is she also here?

05:02.760 --> 05:05.620
I eavesdropped on your schedule,
so I came here.

05:05.620 --> 05:07.680
Wait, what does this mean?
And it's so scary.

05:07.960 --> 05:09.540
I'm really sorry.

05:09.800 --> 05:13.099
I thought I had dealt with all the bugs.

05:13.100 --> 05:15.700
What a pity!

05:15.700 --> 05:17.960
There's still one in the living room.

05:17.960 --> 05:21.820
Don't have professional battles
in places I can't see, okay?

05:22.500 --> 05:24.060
We came out to buy women's wear.

05:24.061 --> 05:26.559
You can't handle it well
on your own, right?

05:26.560 --> 05:29.840
I think even you can't
handle it well either.

05:30.360 --> 05:34.000
This beautiful and cool lady,

05:34.380 --> 05:36.580
are you also an assassin?

05:39.900 --> 05:41.040
Yes.

05:41.580 --> 05:43.900
Please don't lay a hand on Riko.

05:46.820 --> 05:49.800
Mature women smell so good.

05:49.800 --> 05:52.600
You're as funny and cute as Hitoyoshi.

05:52.600 --> 05:53.490
Cute.

05:54.780 --> 05:57.300
Anyway, don't mind them.

05:57.620 --> 06:00.159
Let's go choose Miss Yuki's clothes.

06:00.160 --> 06:01.920
Regarding this,

06:02.140 --> 06:04.960
there's a store nearby
that I highly recommend.

06:04.960 --> 06:05.980
It's Master Riko's…

06:05.980 --> 06:08.020
Then let's go take a look.

06:08.020 --> 06:09.020
Hmm.

06:18.880 --> 06:20.780
Are you ready?

06:21.640 --> 06:22.680
Yes.

06:27.740 --> 06:29.160
Wait, this…

06:30.040 --> 06:32.060
This is even more eye-catching
than the previous one?

06:32.680 --> 06:35.420
Sorry, I can't fight my own desires.

06:36.120 --> 06:37.480
From my perspective,

06:37.480 --> 06:41.340
this outfit seems to be more inconvenient
to move than the previous one.

06:41.340 --> 06:43.180
She's choosing clothes in a standard
of how efficiently she can move.

06:43.440 --> 06:46.340
But it really suits you.

06:46.340 --> 06:47.940
So cute. I love it.

06:47.940 --> 06:48.880
Hey.

06:48.880 --> 06:52.420
Don't forget we came to buy
ordinary clothes for her to wear.

06:52.420 --> 06:54.000
I know.

06:55.580 --> 06:58.139
Then it's my turn.

06:58.140 --> 07:00.820
Let's show you
what a mature woman would wear.

07:05.800 --> 07:08.559
What do you think, Master Hitoyoshi?

07:08.560 --> 07:11.720
It's not appropriate for you
to walk on the street dressed like this!

07:12.000 --> 07:13.240
Indeed.

07:14.080 --> 07:17.479
Wearing this outfit would
make it hard to hide knives.

07:17.480 --> 07:19.856
Is knife storage also a standard?

07:20.720 --> 07:22.740
-That outfit is pretty nice.
-Forget about this outfit.

07:22.740 --> 07:26.380
Since you're no longer engaged in assassinations
don't worry about hiding the knives.

07:26.780 --> 07:28.139
No.

07:28.140 --> 07:30.320
Just having knives

07:30.320 --> 07:32.080
calms my mind.

07:32.460 --> 07:35.400
I'd better not to tell her
that she's not allowed to carry knives.

07:36.540 --> 07:38.560
You two!

07:38.560 --> 07:40.180
If you're not serious,

07:40.180 --> 07:42.240
then can you stop messing around?

07:43.420 --> 07:44.780
Sorry.

07:44.780 --> 07:47.150
Next, let's go to a more normal store.

08:02.500 --> 08:03.520
Wow.

08:03.520 --> 08:06.760
You look good in anything you wear.

08:06.760 --> 08:08.220
You look like a model.

08:08.220 --> 08:10.440
Why is there a swimsuit in the mix?

08:10.440 --> 08:13.559
Hitoyoshi, which one do you like?

08:13.560 --> 08:15.220
Me?

08:16.660 --> 08:22.400
I-I think something like a white one-piece
would suit Miss Yuki very well.

08:23.060 --> 08:25.020
Ah.

08:25.020 --> 08:27.380
That's what you love.

08:27.380 --> 08:30.301
I don't like this person.

08:34.000 --> 08:36.240
It's pretty much done,

08:39.500 --> 08:43.499
but rather than picking out clothes,
it's more like we bought everything she tried on.

08:43.500 --> 08:45.060
It's really hard to decide.

08:46.500 --> 08:48.840
They're having a Halloween sale.

08:48.840 --> 08:53.081
I've heard that Halloween
is a big festival in Japan too.

08:53.082 --> 08:54.380
But this is really something.

08:54.380 --> 08:57.499
It's amazing. There are so many clothes.

08:57.500 --> 09:01.540
Okay, let's choose the clothes
Hitoyoshi would wear this year.

09:01.540 --> 09:02.240
Eh?

09:02.240 --> 09:04.120
Are you also going to celebrate this year?

09:04.120 --> 09:05.320
Of course.

09:05.320 --> 09:07.740
Mom looks forward to it every year.

09:08.699 --> 09:10.520
Wait, wait for me, Riko.

09:11.480 --> 09:14.180
Chick or treat.

09:14.180 --> 09:15.440
It's supposed to be Trick or Treat.

09:19.720 --> 09:22.220
Miss Maid is dressed as a witch.

09:22.800 --> 09:25.760
If you don't give me candy,
I'll arrest you.

09:25.760 --> 09:28.240
It's not about Halloween anymore.

09:28.240 --> 09:30.160
Oh my, so sexy.

09:32.100 --> 09:35.119
Master Riko is very happy.

09:35.120 --> 09:38.220
She dresses up very earnestly every year.

09:41.310 --> 09:42.840
HORROR MOVIE APPRECIATION BATTING DEAD

09:42.840 --> 09:43.680
Ah.

09:44.340 --> 09:47.060
It's that zombie movie

09:47.060 --> 09:47.640
BATTING DEAD
called Batting Dead.

09:47.640 --> 09:50.190
BATTING DEAD
I love it.

09:50.540 --> 09:52.540
That's great.

09:52.540 --> 09:53.840
Let's go watch it together.

09:53.840 --> 09:55.160
Let's go.

09:55.760 --> 09:56.800
Is that okay?

09:57.480 --> 10:00.800
You mean go to the cinema, right?

10:01.220 --> 10:01.980
Eh?

10:02.360 --> 10:04.539
Don't you usually go to the cinema?

10:04.540 --> 10:06.360
Do you like watching movies at home?

10:06.700 --> 10:07.560
Not really.

10:08.140 --> 10:09.500
For me,

10:12.900 --> 10:15.180
going to the cinema

10:15.420 --> 10:19.040
is more often for assassination missions,
not movies.

10:19.780 --> 10:22.580
I rarely watch movies.

10:22.580 --> 10:26.918
After all, cinemas are dim and noisy.

10:30.640 --> 10:32.820
I can't stand staying at such a place.

10:32.820 --> 10:34.980
Wait, you can't go there.

10:41.440 --> 10:42.460
Don't come over.

10:43.240 --> 10:44.780
Don't come over.

11:02.804 --> 11:04.343
Zombies

11:04.360 --> 11:05.540
are so scary.

11:05.820 --> 11:07.939
Zombies are not scary at all.

11:07.940 --> 11:11.060
With your techniques,
you can take them down easily.

11:11.480 --> 11:13.500
R-Right.

11:14.452 --> 11:17.571
Firstly, I can't bear
the stench of the rotting corpses.

11:17.580 --> 11:19.520
Her first thought is quite unique.

11:19.520 --> 11:21.200
And they're already corpses.

11:21.200 --> 11:23.280
Just the thought of them
being unkillable, I…

11:23.740 --> 11:24.840
I see.

11:24.840 --> 11:25.977
Indeed.

11:27.860 --> 11:30.040
For Miss Yuki,

11:30.440 --> 11:33.300
she lives relying on her past experiences.

11:33.880 --> 11:35.620
It's not easy for her to be ordinary.

11:36.520 --> 11:40.720
More importantly,
I have no experience of being a zombie.

11:40.720 --> 11:43.800
Wait. No one has that kind of experience,
so don't worry.

11:44.160 --> 11:47.200
As an assassin, you're afraid of zombies.

11:47.200 --> 11:49.100
That's weird.

11:56.980 --> 11:58.020
Oh.

11:58.020 --> 11:59.400
Hitoyoshi, look.

11:59.400 --> 12:02.320
It's like a treasure chest
of fresh cream inside.

12:02.320 --> 12:04.840
It's really rich.

12:04.840 --> 12:06.580
Can you eat dinner after having this?

12:06.580 --> 12:08.770
Of course.

12:10.960 --> 12:12.680
It's really delicious.

12:12.680 --> 12:14.280
Miss Yuki, do you want to try some?

12:14.280 --> 12:15.760
Can I?

12:15.760 --> 12:16.986
Of course.

12:18.840 --> 12:19.860
How is it?

12:20.280 --> 12:21.783
It's delicious.

12:25.440 --> 12:27.020
Come on.

12:27.020 --> 12:28.580
No need.

12:28.580 --> 12:30.040
I won't eat it.

12:30.040 --> 12:31.700
Then let me feed you.

12:35.640 --> 12:37.400
Here, please have some.

12:37.400 --> 12:38.460
Wait.

12:38.820 --> 12:40.460
How is it? It's delicious, right?

12:40.460 --> 12:42.640
Yes, it is delicious.

12:43.540 --> 12:45.080
You let your guard down, Naka.

12:45.940 --> 12:49.100
You are nothing like someone
who inherits the Hikage.

12:49.480 --> 12:52.299
You have to grasp
the surrounding situation at all times.

12:52.300 --> 12:53.879
Don't let your guard down.

12:53.880 --> 12:56.820
I'm really sorry, Take.

12:57.460 --> 12:59.780
Tonight, let's train your lower body.

13:00.360 --> 13:01.220
Yes.

13:01.540 --> 13:03.908
I am honored.

13:09.040 --> 13:11.180
Shopping is really fun.

13:11.180 --> 13:13.179
Let's go out again sometime, Miss Yuki.

13:13.180 --> 13:14.239
Okay.

13:14.240 --> 13:15.600
You too, Miss Grace.

13:15.600 --> 13:16.400
Sure.

13:16.400 --> 13:18.000
I'm okay to go out with you.

13:18.000 --> 13:19.720
Don't ask Hitoyoshi to come next time.

13:19.720 --> 13:21.940
Let's go shopping, just us girls.

13:21.940 --> 13:24.800
That would make things
a bit easier for me.

13:30.740 --> 13:32.860
Goodbye, Miss Grace.

13:33.100 --> 13:34.340
Goodbye.

13:34.340 --> 13:36.820
I'll take Riko home first.

13:37.140 --> 13:38.400
What about you, Miss Yuki?

13:38.400 --> 13:41.980
Then I'll go back and prepare dinner.

13:41.981 --> 13:43.056
I see.

13:43.057 --> 13:44.407
See you.

13:46.240 --> 13:47.900
See you next time.

15:23.900 --> 15:25.480
Do you want me to play with you?

15:29.900 --> 15:31.320
It's all saliva.

15:33.640 --> 15:36.300
We left this morning,

15:36.840 --> 15:38.980
so I didn't do the laundry.

15:40.060 --> 15:41.940
Even if Master Hitoyoshi is not at home,

15:42.560 --> 15:43.985
I can't neglect the laundry.

15:46.300 --> 15:47.679
Agemochitarou.

15:47.680 --> 15:49.860
I'll take that toy and towel to wash.

15:52.160 --> 15:52.820
Come on.

15:52.820 --> 15:54.480
Agemochitarou.

16:04.200 --> 16:05.240
It's thundering.

16:05.880 --> 16:07.660
Miss Yuki is okay, right?

16:11.800 --> 16:13.500
The power's out.

16:37.600 --> 16:40.583
Was that Agemochitarou's sound just now?

17:20.980 --> 17:22.200
So,

17:24.940 --> 17:28.780
you cut up the towel of Mochitarou
while you were scared, right?

17:29.020 --> 17:30.920
I'm very sorry.

17:33.520 --> 17:34.980
Don't cry, Mochitarou.

17:35.620 --> 17:38.980
Later, I will mend the towel.

17:39.420 --> 17:40.620
Eh?

17:41.340 --> 17:44.410
Can you mend it when you cut it like that?

17:46.440 --> 17:48.760
I will mend it. I'll do my best.

17:49.360 --> 17:50.320
I see.

17:50.740 --> 17:51.596
Mm.

17:51.597 --> 17:53.077
Thank you then.

17:53.680 --> 17:55.760
Mochitarou is happy, right?

17:58.712 --> 17:59.771
Eh?

17:59.780 --> 18:01.684
You've changed back into your maid outfit.

18:03.480 --> 18:04.979
Don't you

18:04.980 --> 18:08.360
like those clothes we bought?

18:09.240 --> 18:11.757
No.

18:12.560 --> 18:16.079
You went shopping with me
and helped me pick out those clothes,

18:16.080 --> 18:17.900
which made me so happy.

18:18.460 --> 18:19.760
But…

18:21.300 --> 18:26.363
You'll take care of me from now on.

18:27.420 --> 18:30.260
That is a gift from me.

18:31.080 --> 18:35.948
This maid outfit is a precious gift
given to me by Master.

18:36.720 --> 18:43.040
It's the only thing that connects me
to Master who's gone.

18:43.760 --> 18:47.240
Since you've chosen not to kill,

18:47.240 --> 18:51.088
I think it's also a good choice, Yuki.

18:51.680 --> 18:53.239
At that time,

18:53.240 --> 18:55.819
I failed to grasp the meaning of that.

18:55.820 --> 19:00.306
I ended up serving Master
as an assassin to the end.

19:00.940 --> 19:02.959
But now,

19:02.960 --> 19:06.979
this maid outfit has led me here.

19:08.560 --> 19:11.500
Even though I know
this outfit is not ordinary,

19:12.060 --> 19:14.605
I still want to keep wearing it.

19:15.200 --> 19:17.907
Is it weird for me to think so?

19:18.820 --> 19:20.260
Not at all.

19:21.020 --> 19:22.060
But,

19:22.060 --> 19:26.759
it's weird that I'm afraid of zombies
when I'm an assassin, right?

19:26.760 --> 19:27.840
Ah.

19:27.840 --> 19:30.860
Miss Grace did say so.

19:31.600 --> 19:34.680
There's nothing weird about it.

19:36.640 --> 19:39.560
To wear what you like,

19:40.132 --> 19:42.871
and to be afraid of anything
that's scared you,

19:42.880 --> 19:43.860
none of these are weird.

19:44.480 --> 19:48.059
But what you like to wear
happens to be a maid outfit.

19:48.060 --> 19:50.439
And what you are afraid of
just happen to be zombies.

19:52.880 --> 19:56.519
Moreover, it's ordinary to have
things you like and things you fear.

19:56.520 --> 20:00.340
And it's ordinary to want
to cherish such feelings.

20:00.740 --> 20:01.959
So,

20:01.960 --> 20:05.930
I think you just have to be yourself.

20:06.980 --> 20:08.380
Be

20:09.120 --> 20:10.420
myself?

20:11.520 --> 20:12.837
Exactly.

20:17.400 --> 20:19.846
Just wait a bit longer, Mochitarou.

20:19.847 --> 20:21.940
We need to go prepare dinner.

20:24.500 --> 20:26.058
Can't you wait?

20:27.580 --> 20:28.380
Eh?

20:28.640 --> 20:29.780
This towel

20:30.080 --> 20:32.780
is the one that was with you
when I found you.

20:33.500 --> 20:36.240
It might have the scent
of your parents on it.

20:37.400 --> 20:40.200
Agemochitarou's family…

20:40.800 --> 20:42.860
Well, Master Hitoyoshi.

20:43.160 --> 20:43.880
Hmm?

20:44.380 --> 20:46.319
Can I try to

20:46.320 --> 20:49.260
mend this towel before dinner?

20:49.520 --> 20:50.519
Eh?

20:50.520 --> 20:51.860
It's okay.

20:52.240 --> 20:55.839
I know how it feels.

20:55.840 --> 20:58.420
Because for me, this bell

20:58.420 --> 21:03.100
is the only thing that connects me
to my sister who is so far apart.

21:03.100 --> 21:04.200
I see.

21:04.200 --> 21:06.500
Your sister who is so far apart.

21:08.540 --> 21:10.860
The thought of losing this…

21:11.800 --> 21:12.960
Sister?

21:17.680 --> 21:20.500
Miss Yuki, do you have a sister?
